# ~/.config/labwc/autostart  --  Guitar Rig Analyzer
#
# Created 2026-09-30 (Tk UI). MIGRATED 2026-10-15 to the web kiosk.
#
# *** labwc 0.20.1 RUNS THIS FILE IN ADDITION TO /etc/xdg/labwc/autostart,
# *** NOT INSTEAD OF IT.
#
# The first version of this file was a copy of the system file minus
# pcmanfm-pi, on the assumption that a user file SHADOWS the system one. It
# does not. The 2026-09-30 reboot test proved it: TWO 'lwrespawn wf-panel-pi'
# supervisors and TWO kanshi processes were running, one set from each file --
# and pcmanfm-pi started anyway, from the system file, which this file cannot
# prevent.
#
# So this file contains ONLY what must be ADDED to the stock session.
# Everything else -- pcmanfm-pi, wf-panel-pi, kanshi, lxsession-xdg-autostart
# -- comes from /etc/xdg/labwc/autostart, which is NOT modified (sha256
# 3a53212ad85afb47ef60ebb66c5a6c911cba210ff5577492acfafa2c68edb719).
#
# ==============================================================================
# 2026-10-15 -- THE PRODUCTION UI IS NOW THE WEB KIOSK (ADR-005 §2)
# ==============================================================================
#
# ADR-005 §2 makes the web client the production default once it can, on the Pi:
#   §2.1 boot directly into Chromium        -- this line
#   §2.2 connect to analyzer_link           -- met 2026-10-13
#   §2.3 render real protocol-v2 frames     -- met 2026-10-13
#   §2.4 survive disconnect and reconnect   -- met 2026-10-15
#        ai/evidence/2026-10-15-pi-web-disconnect-reconnect.md
#
# The Tk line below is COMMENTED, NOT DELETED. ADR-005 §2 retains the Tk
# renderer as the reference/debug renderer -- the one that has been run against
# the real UART on the physical display, and the one a disagreement is
# adjudicated against. Its launcher and the Pi's own checkout are untouched.
#
#   OLD (Tk), kept verbatim for rollback:
# /home/conley/guitar_rig_analyzer/pi/run_ui.sh --serial /dev/ttyAMA0 &
#
# ROLLBACK, COMPLETE AND EXACT, over SSH and with no keyboard:
#
#     sh ~/gra-rollback/restore-tk-startup.sh
#
# which restores this file byte-for-byte to the Tk original
# (sha256 b40fbc70653ccfa53a808b170877f1cc9ab589f6e17d95498064ea5c6f986c60)
# and verifies the hash before and after. To stop the kiosk taking the panel on
# the next boot WITHOUT restoring Tk:
#
#     touch ~/gra-ui/DISABLE_KIOSK_AUTOSTART
#
# WHY A SUPERVISOR AND NOT run_web.sh DIRECTLY: boot needs three things that the
# launcher deliberately does not do -- wait for the compositor socket, retry a
# bounded number of times, and fall back to the Tk UI rather than leave a
# keyboard-less panel blank. run_kiosk_boot.sh adds exactly those and calls the
# same proven run_web.sh underneath. It is NOT a restart loop: retries are
# scoped to startup, so terminating a running kiosk frees /dev/ttyAMA0 and stays
# terminated -- the same operator decision that kept the Tk line out of
# lwrespawn on 2026-09-30.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT WRAPPED IN lwrespawn, unchanged from 2026-09-30:
#   - terminating the UI must free /dev/ttyAMA0 for diagnostics;
#   - a crashing application must not enter a restart loop;
#   - this is a development instrument, not a locked-down appliance.
#
# CODE LOCATION: ~/gra-ui/ is the DURABLE production deployment, byte-identical
# to the repository's pi/ tree. It is deliberately NOT ~/gra-webtest or
# ~/gra-stage-*, which are scratch trees that may be deleted, and NOT
# ~/guitar_rig_analyzer, which is the stale dirty checkout the Tk line used.

/home/conley/gra-ui/pi/run_kiosk_boot.sh &
